hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20803","Surayj and Yunus narrated to us, both said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith al-Laythi, he said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were young men, he said: So we stayed with him for about twenty nights, and he said to us: If you return to your lands, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was merciful, then teach them, Surayj said: And command them to pray such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time, Yunus said: And order them to pray such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time and such-and-such prayer at such-and-such time, and when the prayer comes, let one of you call the adhan for you and let the eldest of you lead you."
"20804","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, and he is Abu Sulayman, that they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he and a companion of his, or two companions of his, and one of them said, two companions of his, Ayyub or Khalid, and he said to them: When the prayer comes, then call the adhan and the iqamah, and let the eldest of you lead you, and pray as you see me pray."
"20805","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Qatadah narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, and he was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands when he entered the prayer, when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, up to his ears."
"20806","Waki' narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah al-Uqayli, from a man among them nicknamed Abu Atiyyah, he said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith used to come to us in our prayer place and converse, he said: One day the prayer came, so we said: Step forward, and he said: No, let one of you step forward until I tell you why I will not step forward: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever visits a people, let him not lead them, but let a man from among them lead them."
"20807","Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj and Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated it to us, both said: Aban narrated to us, Budayl narrated to us, the like of it."
"20808","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar informed us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, Abu Atiyyah, a freedman of ours, narrated to me, he said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith used to come to us in our prayer place, then he mentioned the hadith, meaning the hadith of Abu Atiyyah."
"20809","Abd al-Samad and Abu Amir narrated to us, both said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said the takbir would raise his hands until he placed them close to his ears, and when he bowed he did the like of that, and when he raised his head from bowing he did the like of that."
"20810","Isma'il narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the prayer he raised his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, until they were level with the lobes of his ears."
"20811","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands level with the lobes of his ears in bowing and prostration."
"20812","Affan narrated to us, Aban al-Attar narrated to us, Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, Abu Atiyyah, a freedman among us, narrated to us, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: He used to come to us in our prayer place, and when the prayer was established it was said to him: Step forward and pray, he said: Let one of you pray, until I tell you why I will not pray with you as imam; when the people had prayed, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you visits a people, let him not pray with them as imam; a man from among them prays with them."
"20813","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith al-Laythi, that he said to his companions one day: Shall I not show you how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was? He said: And that was at other than a prayer time; so he stood and stood firmly, then bowed and bowed firmly, then raised his head and stood upright for a while, then prostrated, then raised his head, and he said the takbir while sitting, then waited a while, then prostrated. Abu Qilabah said: So he prayed a prayer like the prayer of this shaykh of ours, meaning Amr ibn Salamah al-Jarmi, and he used to lead in prayer at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ayyub said: And I saw Amr ibn Salamah doing something I do not see you doing: when he raised his head from the two prostrations, he sat upright, then stood from the first and second rak'ah."
